1
00:00:54,208 --> 00:00:55,833
Take your medicine, dear.

2
00:01:20,041 --> 00:01:21,666
The rain smells nice.

3
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:24,541
Once it's over,

4
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:27,041
shall we go for a walk?

5
00:01:34,791 --> 00:01:37,000
Take your medicine, then we'll go.

6
00:03:13,125 --> 00:03:13,958
Inspector.

7
00:03:15,416 --> 00:03:17,916
Forensics is on their way, almost here.

8
00:03:21,166 --> 00:03:23,333
Has this crime scene been photographed?

9
00:03:23,416 --> 00:03:25,166
Yep, all done, sir.

10
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:29,000
Phii Pong!

11
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:32,625
It's Phii Pong! Narong is Phii Pong!

12
00:03:32,708 --> 00:03:34,791
If they locked him up,

13
00:03:34,875 --> 00:03:37,125
Shaman Sak wouldn't be dead!

14
00:03:42,666 --> 00:03:44,416
This is revenge.

15
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:47,208
Shaman Sak knew!

16
00:03:47,291 --> 00:03:49,458
He knew Narong is Phii Pong!

17
00:04:01,250 --> 00:04:02,458
Don't worry.

18
00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:05,291
Everything will work itself out.

19
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
DELUSION

20
00:05:36,083 --> 00:05:37,333
The case you made,

21
00:05:37,958 --> 00:05:39,791
for Mued's killer was pretty strong.

22
00:05:41,791 --> 00:05:43,583
Until your suspect was killed, too.

23
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:46,958
Yes, sir. But maybe he didn't act alone.

24
00:05:47,833 --> 00:05:49,833
Someone else knows about the body.

25
00:05:51,833 --> 00:05:53,000
Everyone…

26
00:05:53,083 --> 00:05:54,333
knows about that kid.

27
00:05:55,375 --> 00:05:57,666
Ever since the Phii Pong case years ago.

28
00:06:00,541 --> 00:06:03,166
And the cases you
found in other provinces.

29
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:05,125
Plan of attack?

30
00:06:09,833 --> 00:06:11,708
Sounds like we'll close one case,

31
00:06:12,541 --> 00:06:13,666
but open a new one.

32
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:18,375
I'd rather you didn't complicate
things with cases from other provinces.

33
00:06:19,083 --> 00:06:21,916
When the evidence doesn't
seem to be linked at all.

34
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,500
We have to figure out
who killed Sak and that's…

35
00:06:26,333 --> 00:06:28,166
enough of a headache for us already.

36
00:06:28,250 --> 00:06:30,375
I just need more time, sir.

37
00:06:32,291 --> 00:06:33,500
I'll give you that

38
00:06:34,291 --> 00:06:36,375
but don't let this become a thing

39
00:06:36,458 --> 00:06:38,416
that blows up on the news.

40
00:06:39,041 --> 00:06:41,958
The messier things get,
the harder it is to finish the job.

41
00:06:44,708 --> 00:06:45,791
Here.

42
00:06:48,750 --> 00:06:50,750
But, do me a favor and be careful, okay?

43
00:06:51,875 --> 00:06:52,791
Yes, sir.

44
00:07:13,958 --> 00:07:15,583
They can't release the body.

45
00:07:17,041 --> 00:07:18,250
Till the autopsy.

46
00:07:19,666 --> 00:07:20,541
Now what, Mom?

47
00:07:23,666 --> 00:07:24,875
I'm done waiting.

48
00:07:25,666 --> 00:07:27,083
Let's go ahead…

49
00:07:28,250 --> 00:07:29,875
with the funeral.

50
00:07:30,375 --> 00:07:32,916
I'm the only family he's got.

51
00:07:39,875 --> 00:07:41,375
How many days, Mom?

52
00:07:44,250 --> 00:07:47,125
Three days… is enough.

53
00:07:50,250 --> 00:07:52,125
Did Dad go out that night?

54
00:07:54,333 --> 00:07:55,166
Oh, you--

55
00:07:56,625 --> 00:07:58,375
You think your dad did this?

56
00:07:59,291 --> 00:08:00,833
I was just asking.

57
00:08:01,375 --> 00:08:02,500
Can we go now?

58
00:08:03,375 --> 00:08:06,250
I'll need to head off
to the temple to sort things out.

59
00:08:22,166 --> 00:08:23,958
- Hello?
<i>- Mrs. Wan?</i>

60
00:08:24,041 --> 00:08:26,208
<i>It's Supattra, Mr. Yote's attorney.</i>

61
00:08:26,291 --> 00:08:27,375
Yes.

62
00:08:27,458 --> 00:08:29,666
<i>I'm calling about the mediation date.</i>

63
00:08:31,041 --> 00:08:33,208
<i>Your attorney hasn't</i>
<i>gotten back to us yet.</i>

64
00:08:36,625 --> 00:08:38,625
I've just had a lot on.

65
00:08:38,708 --> 00:08:40,875
I'll get back to you when I can.

66
00:08:40,958 --> 00:08:42,625
<i>Well, please don't take too long.</i>

67
00:08:42,708 --> 00:08:44,791
<i>I don't want this to have to go to court.</i>

68
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:48,791
<i>We don't want to have to bring up</i>
<i>what happened between your father and Aim.</i>

69
00:08:48,875 --> 00:08:50,083
<i>Do we?</i>

70
00:09:11,416 --> 00:09:12,375
Inspector.

71
00:09:13,041 --> 00:09:14,041
Look at this.

72
00:09:17,916 --> 00:09:20,541
The neighbor and Saeng's boy
filmed this last night.

73
00:09:21,208 --> 00:09:23,375
He heard Grandpa Narong shouting.

74
00:09:24,875 --> 00:09:28,750
<i>Ghosts in the forest! Don't go in!</i>

75
00:09:28,833 --> 00:09:30,833
- <i>There are ghosts here!</i>
- Where is he now?

76
00:09:30,916 --> 00:09:32,250
With the duty officer.

77
00:09:33,125 --> 00:09:35,000
Can you keep a copy of this?

78
00:09:35,708 --> 00:09:36,833
Already done.

79
00:09:36,916 --> 00:09:37,750
Thank you.

80
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:12,250
ANUPONG'S PHOTO

81
00:10:13,166 --> 00:10:15,375
PACHARA JUNSAYPUN
PORNCHAI JAMROON

82
00:10:15,458 --> 00:10:17,458
SAK SONGSIPHAN

83
00:10:55,625 --> 00:10:56,750
Hello there, ma'am.

84
00:11:10,916 --> 00:11:12,291
Counsellor.

85
00:11:14,375 --> 00:11:16,333
Ah, my condolences.

86
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,375
I'm sure the police will
do everything they can.

87
00:11:19,458 --> 00:11:21,291
To find out who did this,

88
00:11:21,375 --> 00:11:22,833
and catch them soon.

89
00:11:25,250 --> 00:11:27,458
Please take this for the funeral.

90
00:11:32,375 --> 00:11:35,041
The Shaman lived all by himself.

91
00:11:35,125 --> 00:11:36,750
It's a big part of land.

92
00:11:37,583 --> 00:11:40,291
He must have had some
other relatives though, right?

93
00:11:41,166 --> 00:11:42,208
No.

94
00:11:42,291 --> 00:11:45,541
I guess the land is all
yours in that case.

95
00:11:47,750 --> 00:11:49,250
A blessing and a curse.

96
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,166
I don't really know
about those things, sir.

97
00:11:54,541 --> 00:11:56,333
Well, I'm here to deliver

98
00:11:56,416 --> 00:11:59,583
the land mortgage agreement to you.

99
00:12:04,458 --> 00:12:07,958
He mortgaged it with me
for over 200,000 baht.

100
00:12:08,041 --> 00:12:10,000
And he paid back almost nothing.

101
00:12:10,083 --> 00:12:12,500
Now, the interest is almost double that.

102
00:12:12,583 --> 00:12:17,500
I'll round it down to 350,000 baht.

103
00:12:17,583 --> 00:12:21,916
Pay this back
and I can give you back your land.

104
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,500
I understand it's a bad situation.

105
00:12:24,583 --> 00:12:28,250
You didn't even spend the money
and you're left with the debt.

106
00:12:28,333 --> 00:12:31,291
We all have to follow
the law though, right?

107
00:12:32,291 --> 00:12:33,916
I don't want this to…

108
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,625
end up in court.

109
00:12:35,708 --> 00:12:37,375
We're like a family here.

110
00:12:45,208 --> 00:12:46,291
So--

111
00:12:46,375 --> 00:12:47,875
Inspector?

112
00:12:49,541 --> 00:12:50,375
Not here.

113
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:54,916
- Sergeant.
- Oh! Yes, sir?

114
00:12:56,041 --> 00:12:59,333
If we disregard the teeth,
could it be the same killer?

115
00:13:01,833 --> 00:13:03,458
Uh…

116
00:13:06,041 --> 00:13:07,541
Got this for you.

117
00:13:29,708 --> 00:13:30,875
Hmm.

118
00:13:43,208 --> 00:13:44,666
Roughly speaking,

119
00:13:46,083 --> 00:13:48,041
looks like this hut's within

120
00:13:48,125 --> 00:13:50,750
the boundaries of Narong's property.

121
00:13:50,833 --> 00:13:52,833
71 YEARS OLD, MEMORY IMPAIRMENT, SUSPECT

122
00:13:59,458 --> 00:14:00,625
Where are you going?

123
00:14:01,583 --> 00:14:03,666
The temple, to make merit.

124
00:14:05,833 --> 00:14:07,583
Why are you in black then?

125
00:14:08,375 --> 00:14:10,750
People don't wear black to make merit.

126
00:14:12,416 --> 00:14:15,583
Won't be long.
I'll bring something to eat.

127
00:14:31,291 --> 00:14:34,958
<i>Ghosts in the forest! Don't go in!</i>

128
00:14:37,083 --> 00:14:38,666
If he needs to pee,

129
00:14:38,750 --> 00:14:40,250
or walk around,

130
00:14:40,916 --> 00:14:43,375
I let him out at night
for ten minutes or so.

131
00:14:43,458 --> 00:14:46,083
After that, he's tied up till morning.

132
00:14:47,041 --> 00:14:49,333
You can just tie him up by yourself?

133
00:14:51,333 --> 00:14:56,416
Oh, we can tie him up when he's sleeping,
or really out of it, from the mat.

134
00:14:58,041 --> 00:14:58,875
Hmm.

135
00:15:01,625 --> 00:15:03,041
Or maybe you're lying.

136
00:15:07,083 --> 00:15:09,166
Which means I can't help him.

137
00:15:10,291 --> 00:15:11,333
Help him?

138
00:15:11,416 --> 00:15:12,541
Whatever for?

139
00:15:15,041 --> 00:15:17,291
Were you aware of enemies
your brother had?

140
00:15:17,375 --> 00:15:19,083
To end up dead, like Mued.

141
00:15:19,666 --> 00:15:22,166
You think it was my husband?
Then arrest him.

142
00:15:22,791 --> 00:15:25,083
Mom… don't. Don't.

143
00:15:27,625 --> 00:15:29,291
Whatever else you need…

144
00:15:29,375 --> 00:15:31,416
you go ask him, I'm busy.

145
00:15:32,666 --> 00:15:34,125
That's all right.

146
00:15:35,458 --> 00:15:36,666
I'll let him rest.

147
00:15:38,208 --> 00:15:40,291
But I'm counting on you to keep him here.

148
00:15:40,875 --> 00:15:42,666
Don't let him wander off.

149
00:15:43,666 --> 00:15:45,333
Uncle Sak's case is still open.

150
00:15:45,958 --> 00:15:48,333
Don't want people calling him a ghost.

151
00:15:52,125 --> 00:15:54,833
Okay, Mom, let's go inside,
I'll take you to the temple.

152
00:15:57,208 --> 00:15:58,458
She was lying.

153
00:15:59,125 --> 00:16:01,541
Her lip trembled, see that?

154
00:16:03,333 --> 00:16:06,000
LAWYER SUPATTRA:
IF YOU CANNOT SCHEDULE THE MEDIATION,

155
00:16:06,083 --> 00:16:09,583
MR. YOTE WILL FILE FOR DIVORCE
AND PRESS CHARGES AGAINST MR. NARONG.

156
00:16:19,833 --> 00:16:21,875
- Mosquitos?
- Mmm.

157
00:16:23,291 --> 00:16:25,833
Ah, here. Mm?

158
00:16:27,458 --> 00:16:28,500
There.

159
00:16:29,333 --> 00:16:30,541
You look upset.

160
00:16:31,125 --> 00:16:32,250
Something wrong?

161
00:16:33,875 --> 00:16:34,708
I'm fine.

162
00:16:36,833 --> 00:16:38,708
Beat the boss in your game?

163
00:16:39,291 --> 00:16:40,291
Huh?

164
00:16:40,875 --> 00:16:42,708
The one with the slashes.

165
00:16:43,375 --> 00:16:44,875
- I did.
- Oh!

166
00:16:45,875 --> 00:16:47,000
Did you get mad?

167
00:16:47,083 --> 00:16:48,250
No way!

168
00:16:51,083 --> 00:16:52,208
Mmm.

169
00:16:54,375 --> 00:16:55,750
Do you miss me yet?

170
00:16:56,291 --> 00:16:57,333
Mmm-hmm.

171
00:17:02,208 --> 00:17:03,125
Mom.

172
00:17:04,250 --> 00:17:05,291
Hmm?

173
00:17:05,375 --> 00:17:07,791
I got into a Bangkok school.

174
00:17:08,416 --> 00:17:11,166
Dad said he wants me to start
middle of next term.

175
00:17:14,541 --> 00:17:15,375
Oh.

176
00:17:28,708 --> 00:17:32,375
Well, I guess I should
look for a job in Bangkok, hmm?

177
00:17:33,833 --> 00:17:35,125
You being away…

178
00:17:36,333 --> 00:17:38,166
I think I might die.

179
00:17:43,208 --> 00:17:47,500
I'll tell Dad to wait
till you get a job first.

180
00:17:47,583 --> 00:17:48,583
Then I'll go.

181
00:17:58,083 --> 00:17:59,708
Well, Bangkok's pretty nice.

182
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,750
Good facilities,

183
00:18:02,833 --> 00:18:04,416
and great sights.

184
00:18:04,958 --> 00:18:06,666
I'm sure you'll love it.

185
00:18:13,416 --> 00:18:15,708
Should we get some ice cream then? Huh?

186
00:18:17,291 --> 00:18:18,500
Then I'll drop you back.

187
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:21,750
- Good?
- Yeah.

188
00:18:29,416 --> 00:18:30,250
Mom!

189
00:18:31,833 --> 00:18:32,666
Mom.

190
00:18:33,333 --> 00:18:35,750
We're not really getting
ice cream, are we?

191
00:18:37,750 --> 00:18:40,458
If you're going to Grandpa's house,
I don't wanna come.

192
00:18:48,958 --> 00:18:49,958
Why not, Aim?

193
00:18:54,208 --> 00:18:55,416
Because we're poor?

194
00:18:56,583 --> 00:18:57,708
Or is it something else?

195
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,583
What did you tell your Dad?

196
00:19:01,333 --> 00:19:02,791
Aim, tell me what happened.

197
00:19:04,041 --> 00:19:05,583
I didn't tell.

198
00:19:06,333 --> 00:19:07,291
Aim.

199
00:19:08,666 --> 00:19:10,083
Please don't lie.

200
00:19:11,166 --> 00:19:13,250
Don't lie to me!

201
00:19:16,250 --> 00:19:17,250
Aim, come on!

202
00:19:18,208 --> 00:19:19,083
What did you say?

203
00:19:20,291 --> 00:19:21,250
Huh?

204
00:19:22,166 --> 00:19:24,791
Grandpa pushed me into the water.

205
00:19:24,875 --> 00:19:28,083
He-- He wasn't making any sense!

206
00:19:28,166 --> 00:19:30,041
It was scary!

207
00:19:33,833 --> 00:19:34,916
Aim…

208
00:19:39,750 --> 00:19:44,458
Why didn't you tell the police?
Why didn't you tell me this before? Huh?

209
00:19:44,541 --> 00:19:47,791
So Dad wouldn't get mad at you!

210
00:19:59,083 --> 00:20:00,416
Aim…

211
00:20:02,083 --> 00:20:04,958
Don't cry now. You did nothing wrong.

212
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:11,166
I'm sorry for getting angry.

213
00:20:16,083 --> 00:20:18,458
Now, let's go back to Dad, hmm?

214
00:20:18,541 --> 00:20:19,666
Before he worries.

215
00:20:22,333 --> 00:20:24,708
See you at your red belt test, okay?

216
00:20:26,208 --> 00:20:27,500
Mmm.

217
00:20:27,583 --> 00:20:28,791
See you then, little boy.

218
00:20:33,375 --> 00:20:34,875
See you then.

219
00:21:57,541 --> 00:21:58,708
Why is he here?

220
00:22:09,666 --> 00:22:11,666
BORN 14 MAY 1962
DIED 18 NOVEMBER 2026

221
00:22:20,541 --> 00:22:21,541
NEVER TO WAKE

222
00:22:22,250 --> 00:22:24,250
NEVER TO RETURN

223
00:22:42,083 --> 00:22:43,666
For you.

224
00:22:43,750 --> 00:22:44,750
Oh, thank you.

225
00:22:49,708 --> 00:22:51,125
Take your dad home.

226
00:22:51,208 --> 00:22:53,000
Who knows when this will end.

227
00:22:53,083 --> 00:22:54,666
I'll get someone to give me a lift.

228
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:58,000
Well go on, go home.

229
00:23:13,750 --> 00:23:15,000
Thanks so much.

230
00:23:15,083 --> 00:23:16,541
No, of course.

231
00:23:17,250 --> 00:23:19,958
Your house is right next door,
we're family, right?

232
00:23:22,208 --> 00:23:23,625
Narong has new pills.

233
00:23:24,250 --> 00:23:25,791
He's really improved.

234
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:29,041
And he didn't kill Mued.

235
00:23:29,666 --> 00:23:31,291
Didn't the police tell you that?

236
00:23:31,375 --> 00:23:32,500
They did.

237
00:23:32,583 --> 00:23:35,958
So, stop sticking your nose
in our business.

238
00:23:37,458 --> 00:23:39,833
You worry about your own family.

239
00:24:14,750 --> 00:24:16,083
Stressed out about family?

240
00:24:17,708 --> 00:24:19,083
Well, you don't need to be.

241
00:24:19,875 --> 00:24:21,541
Your family's rolling in it.

242
00:24:21,625 --> 00:24:23,541
That sounds crazy. Make your point.

243
00:24:23,625 --> 00:24:24,791
So this is a surprise?

244
00:24:27,541 --> 00:24:29,333
Your family owns lots of land.

245
00:24:33,291 --> 00:24:34,750
Even Uncle Sak's house

246
00:24:35,500 --> 00:24:36,375
is yours.

247
00:24:37,666 --> 00:24:39,875
The Phii Pong forest as well.

248
00:24:43,750 --> 00:24:46,375
And now your dad is sick
and your uncle's dead.

249
00:24:47,500 --> 00:24:49,583
Your mom might be the only one who knows.

250
00:24:56,750 --> 00:24:57,916
Seriously?

251
00:24:59,416 --> 00:25:01,291
If you think they did it, arrest them.

252
00:25:03,708 --> 00:25:06,333
But don't ask me.
I don't know what you're talking about.

253
00:25:07,958 --> 00:25:08,958
Her daughter…

254
00:25:10,541 --> 00:25:12,750
and this is the first I've heard of it.

255
00:25:18,416 --> 00:25:20,791
You think your brother
knows about the land?

256
00:25:21,708 --> 00:25:23,458
Don't know.

257
00:25:26,208 --> 00:25:27,458
Okay, I'm done.

258
00:25:30,208 --> 00:25:31,625
If anything changes…

259
00:25:32,750 --> 00:25:36,458
I'll get in touch if I happen
to need anything else, okay?

260
00:25:38,166 --> 00:25:39,458
That's all.

261
00:25:59,958 --> 00:26:01,166
Keep it down.

262
00:26:01,250 --> 00:26:02,250
He's sleeping.

263
00:26:38,416 --> 00:26:40,875
- What are you looking for?
- The deeds.

264
00:26:42,125 --> 00:26:43,791
Or anything that can be sold.

265
00:26:58,208 --> 00:26:59,333
This is what you want.

266
00:26:59,416 --> 00:27:00,416
LAND TITLE DEED

267
00:27:12,750 --> 00:27:14,958
Why did you give Dad's land to Uncle Sak?

268
00:27:17,791 --> 00:27:19,708
Didn't think about your own grandkids?

269
00:27:21,541 --> 00:27:22,958
Mind your business.

270
00:27:23,041 --> 00:27:24,250
Why do you care now?

271
00:27:25,916 --> 00:27:27,250
You never…

272
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:29,583
even thought to tell me?

273
00:27:30,958 --> 00:27:32,666
Were you saving it all for Wat?

274
00:27:34,958 --> 00:27:37,375
You know nothing, shut your mouth.

275
00:27:37,458 --> 00:27:38,291
Don't meddle.

276
00:27:38,958 --> 00:27:40,416
I don't want to!

277
00:27:42,166 --> 00:27:43,875
But when something goes wrong…

278
00:27:45,208 --> 00:27:46,083
it's me!

279
00:27:47,625 --> 00:27:49,291
I have to clean up your shit!

280
00:27:50,416 --> 00:27:52,000
So go back to your house!

281
00:27:52,958 --> 00:27:54,166
We're fine.

282
00:27:55,791 --> 00:27:57,583
Why do you hate me so much?

283
00:27:58,750 --> 00:27:59,583
Hmm?

284
00:28:02,625 --> 00:28:05,750
The only reason I married
that fucking asshole

285
00:28:07,583 --> 00:28:11,375
was so I could save
my family from being poor!

286
00:28:12,708 --> 00:28:16,333
Did you never think
about what I had to sacrifice?

287
00:28:20,958 --> 00:28:24,000
Everything I've done has been for you!

288
00:28:25,875 --> 00:28:27,500
And I've never gotten…

289
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:31,000
a single thank you.

290
00:28:32,875 --> 00:28:33,916
So what?

291
00:28:34,791 --> 00:28:38,041
Nobody's ever thanked me, either.

292
00:28:46,583 --> 00:28:47,750
Well, thank you.

293
00:29:08,500 --> 00:29:11,333
Setting the cases
in other provinces aside,

294
00:29:11,416 --> 00:29:13,500
the suspects right now

295
00:29:13,583 --> 00:29:15,750
are all members of Narong's family.

296
00:29:16,583 --> 00:29:18,875
The first Phii Pong murder happened

297
00:29:18,958 --> 00:29:20,916
on Narong's property.

298
00:29:21,708 --> 00:29:24,875
Near a hut the family claim
they don't know the owner of.

299
00:29:26,083 --> 00:29:27,208
That same year,

300
00:29:28,083 --> 00:29:29,833
Narong passed this land over

301
00:29:30,750 --> 00:29:31,583
to Sak.

302
00:29:33,541 --> 00:29:34,875
Pannee's older brother.

303
00:29:34,958 --> 00:29:36,750
But with no payment, huh?

304
00:29:36,833 --> 00:29:38,375
Here's what I think.

305
00:29:39,500 --> 00:29:41,125
The first Phii Pong murder,

306
00:29:41,208 --> 00:29:42,500
and Mued's murder,

307
00:29:43,791 --> 00:29:46,750
I think might have been the same killer.

308
00:29:47,333 --> 00:29:48,708
But I think, Sak…

309
00:29:49,250 --> 00:29:51,166
was murdered by someone else.

310
00:29:53,166 --> 00:29:55,708
As for all the murders
where teeth are missing…

311
00:29:56,958 --> 00:30:01,333
which resemble the Phii Pong cases,
but happened in other provinces…

312
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:06,583
whoever that killer is,

313
00:30:08,166 --> 00:30:10,708
must have some connection to this family.

314
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:55,833
Nee?

315
00:31:01,666 --> 00:31:02,500
Nee.

316
00:31:08,666 --> 00:31:09,916
Why are you awake?

317
00:31:13,250 --> 00:31:14,625
Is Sak here somewhere?

318
00:31:21,041 --> 00:31:21,875
Mmm-hmm.

319
00:31:38,708 --> 00:31:39,916
Tell him to go home.

320
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:42,750
He's got enough.

321
00:31:44,208 --> 00:31:45,791
We've given so much.

322
00:31:52,291 --> 00:31:53,625
He's got your land.

323
00:31:57,375 --> 00:31:59,000
What else does he want?

324
00:32:07,375 --> 00:32:09,208
We need to stop, Pannee.

325
00:32:10,333 --> 00:32:11,583
I've had enough.

326
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:46,958
Come on!

327
00:32:54,791 --> 00:32:55,833
Pa!

328
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:29,833
Pa!

329
00:33:54,458 --> 00:33:56,333
You called the police right?

330
00:33:59,583 --> 00:34:01,166
No? Why?

331
00:34:01,250 --> 00:34:02,666
I…

332
00:34:02,750 --> 00:34:03,875
I told you!

333
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:06,666
What if someone really dies?

334
00:34:06,750 --> 00:34:08,125
What do we do?

335
00:34:20,541 --> 00:34:21,791
Wait! Pa!

336
00:34:23,083 --> 00:34:24,000
Pa!

337
00:34:24,083 --> 00:34:24,916
Pa!

338
00:35:30,916 --> 00:35:32,541
I'm so sorry, kid!

339
00:35:34,833 --> 00:35:36,500
Pa! Pa, come on! Stop!

340
00:35:36,583 --> 00:35:38,333
I'm sorry.

341
00:35:38,416 --> 00:35:40,958
I'm so sorry! I'm sorry!

342
00:35:45,208 --> 00:35:46,291
I'm sorry…

343
00:37:27,916 --> 00:37:30,041
Hey Sak, the rake now.

344
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:04,916
Let's stop,

345
00:38:06,708 --> 00:38:08,666
before anyone else dies.

346
00:38:09,875 --> 00:38:11,333
Let's talk to the police.

347
00:38:12,625 --> 00:38:15,291
And, we won't have to lie anymore.

348
00:38:18,125 --> 00:38:19,000
I'm tired.

349
00:38:22,416 --> 00:38:23,375
Who?

350
00:38:26,875 --> 00:38:28,125
Who's doing it now?

351
00:38:33,166 --> 00:38:34,791
If you don't give it to me,

352
00:38:34,875 --> 00:38:38,208
I'll go to the police,
let them arrest us all.

353
00:38:55,416 --> 00:38:56,500
Hmm.

354
00:39:00,458 --> 00:39:01,458
Hmm.

355
00:40:07,541 --> 00:40:08,833
Paw.

356
00:40:08,916 --> 00:40:09,875
Paw.

357
00:40:13,458 --> 00:40:15,333
He's gone into the forest again!

358
00:40:16,083 --> 00:40:17,708
You've got to go bring him back!

359
00:40:19,083 --> 00:40:20,000
What?

360
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:21,875
No! No no!

361
00:40:23,250 --> 00:40:24,500
He can't go in there!

362
00:40:26,250 --> 00:40:28,541
We can't let him go in there!

363
00:40:32,958 --> 00:40:34,833
But, don't be scared!

364
00:40:36,041 --> 00:40:36,916
Don't worry.

365
00:40:38,083 --> 00:40:39,375
I'll take care of it.

366
00:40:55,708 --> 00:40:59,291
Ghosts in the forest! Don't go in!

367
00:40:59,375 --> 00:41:03,000
There are ghosts in the forest!
Don't go in there!

368
00:41:46,083 --> 00:41:47,000
Pa!

369
00:41:48,458 --> 00:41:49,833
Pa!

370
00:41:53,333 --> 00:41:54,625
Get away!

371
00:41:55,458 --> 00:41:57,666
- Let me go!
- Go away!

372
00:42:01,208 --> 00:42:02,833
Get him away!

373
00:42:05,916 --> 00:42:07,458
Let me deal with this!

374
00:42:08,291 --> 00:42:09,375
Ma?

375
00:42:11,916 --> 00:42:13,333
What are you doing?

376
00:42:14,916 --> 00:42:16,791
Let's get out of here!
Let's go now!

377
00:42:18,541 --> 00:42:22,208
You don't know! All the things I've done
for you!

378
00:42:23,958 --> 00:42:26,791
- Phii Pong! You're the ghost!
- Yeah!

379
00:42:28,791 --> 00:42:32,125
I am! I am! It's always been me!

380
00:42:32,208 --> 00:42:33,833
Now get out, you two leave!

381
00:42:40,875 --> 00:42:42,083
Come on, Pa!

382
00:43:04,125 --> 00:43:05,833
I'm sorry.

383
00:43:07,958 --> 00:43:09,791
It hurts!

384
00:43:09,875 --> 00:43:11,000
It hurts!

385
00:43:11,083 --> 00:43:12,041
Nee!

386
00:43:16,541 --> 00:43:18,208
Help me.
